<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3558" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-θίνιον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῑ], τό</span>, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Ph.</u>
			282
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Th.
			1.132
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Lg.</u>
			946b
		</span></i>; mostly pl.<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-θίνια</span></b> 
		or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρό-θῑνα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>N.</u>
			7.41
		</span></i>, al.: sg.<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρο-θις</span></b> ,
			ἡ, acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					2561
				</span></i>
			 D <i><span class="en">
				47
			</span></i> Rüsch (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρος, θίς</span>):—<i>topmost</i>
			or <i>best part of heap</i>; hence, <i>firstfruits of the field,
				booty</i>, etc., offered to the gods, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				90
			</span></i>, al., Pi.l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῆς Μαραθῶνι μάχης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					1117
				</span></i>
			 (Delph.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρόθινα
			πολέμου</span>, in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				2.4
			</span></i>, of the Olympic games, <i>as founded from spoils taken in
				war</i>, cf. ib.<i><span class="en">
				10(11).57
			</span></i>.—Properly neut. Adj., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				834
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκροθίνια θύη</span> offerings <i>of
				firstfruits.</i> Post-<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, rare in early Prose.</div>
